//api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8917","id":1333904638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85PgcT-","user":{"login":"CaselIT","id":16175304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTc1MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16175304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT","html_url":"https://github.com/CaselIT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-01T15:05:39Z","updated_at":"2022-12-01T15:39:18Z","body":"On second look it seems that pyodbc is trying to do the opposite, so string to int, even if the type is a string.\r\n\r\n> Conversion failed when converting the nvarchar value 'a' to data type int.\r\n\r\nNot sure why it's trying to do that","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1333904638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"CaselIT","id":16175304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTc1MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16175304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT","html_url":"https://github.com/CaselIT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1333915221","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8917#issuecomment-1333915221","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8917","id":1333915221,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85Pge5V","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-01T15:11:28Z","updated_at":"2022-12-01T15:11:28Z","body":"> ### Describe the bug\r\n> \r\n> When using `fast_executemany` and doing effectively a bulk_insert t we get an error for 2.0.0b3. This works on the 1.4.x branch.\r\n\r\nYes I would recommend not using fast_executemany.  See https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/20/dialects/mssql.html#fast-executemany-mode\r\n\r\n> \r\n> ### Error\r\n\r\nthe stack trace here is not totally expected, but fast_executemany highly modifies how things work so this may be because we aren't turning off setinputsizes().    \r\n\r\nFor the issue here, we should add more notes to the migration log and maybe see if we can fix this trace, however, I would advise walking away from fast_executemany overall as SQLAlchemy's feature is expected to be much more robust.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1333915221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":7932876453,"node_id":"RTE_lADOCX5JB85XtMXkzwAAAAHY1hal","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/7932876453","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"renamed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-12-01T15:12:19Z","rename":{"from":"Change of Behavior: MSSQL insert with fast_executemany failing when mixing int and str values","to":"add fast_executemany deprecation to 2.0 changelog notes; investigate possible API mis-use when it's enabled w/ bulk (add tests?)"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":7932878821,"node_id":"MIE_lADOCX5JB85XtMXkzwAAAAHY1h_l","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/7932878821","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"milestoned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-12-01T15:12:34Z","milestone":{"title":"2.0 final"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1334411102","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8917#issuecomment-1334411102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8917","id":1334411102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85PiX9e","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-01T20:31:27Z","updated_at":"2022-12-01T20:31:27Z","body":"OK here is what happens.\r\n\r\nThe statement that SQL server wont do without extra steps is this:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nconn = engine.raw_connection()\r\ncursor = conn.cursor()\r\ncursor.execute(\"SET IDENTITY_INSERT [user] ON\")\r\n\r\ncursor.execute(\"\"\"\r\n     INSERT INTO [user] (user_id, test, user_name) VALUES (?, ?, ?), (?, ?, ?)\r\n\"\"\", (1, 1, 'a', 2, 1, 5))\r\n```\r\n\r\nany other version of this statement succeeds - if you put 5 for the string as just one row, it succeeds or use executemany(), etc.    so in 1.4 there's no way to reproduce the error without just running the exact statement above.\r\n\r\nin 2.0, the above statement is what insertmanyvalues does.     however, in 2.0 we also turn on use_setinputsizes by default now also.  so using setinputsizes allows the above statement to work:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nconn = engine.raw_connection()\r\ncursor = conn.cursor()\r\ncursor.execute(\"SET IDENTITY_INSERT [user] ON\")\r\n\r\ncursor.setinputsizes([\r\n    (pyodbc.SQL_INTEGER, None, None),\r\n    (pyodbc.SQL_INTEGER, None, None),\r\n    (pyodbc.SQL_VARCHAR, None, None),\r\n    (pyodbc.SQL_INTEGER, None, None),\r\n    (pyodbc.SQL_INTEGER, None, None),\r\n    (pyodbc.SQL_VARCHAR, None, None),\r\n])\r\n\r\ncursor.execute(\"\"\"\r\n     INSERT INTO [user] (user_id, test, user_name) VALUES (?, ?, ?), (?, ?, ?)\r\n\"\"\", (1, 1, 'a', 2, 1, 5))\r\n```\r\n\r\nSQLAlchemy 2.0 will fail if we turn off the setinputsizes step as well:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nengine = create_engine(\r\n    con_str,\r\n    use_setinputsizes=False,\r\n    echo=True)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhere there is in fact a slight bug, is that in 2.0 we also made it so that if fast_executemany is on, we automatically skip \"setinputsizes\" for an executemany(), since this is known to be buggy in pyodbc.    The bug is, that check is not honoring that we are in fact going to do an insertmanyvalues, not a real \"executemany\". \r\n\r\nthis is the fix\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/connectors/pyodbc.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/connectors/pyodbc.py\r\nindex f920860cd8..e8fbed18eb 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/connectors/pyodbc.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/connectors/pyodbc.py\r\n@@ -209,7 +209,10 @@ class PyODBCConnector(Connector):\r\n         # omit the setinputsizes calls for .executemany() with\r\n         # fast_executemany=True\r\n \r\n-        if context.executemany and self.fast_executemany:\r\n+        if (\r\n+            context.execute_style is interfaces.ExecuteStyle.EXECUTEMANY\r\n+            and self.fast_executemany\r\n+        ):\r\n             return\r\n \r\n         cursor.setinputsizes(\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1334411102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":7935490050,"node_id":"UNLE_lADOCX5JB85XtMXkzwAAAAHY_fgC","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/7935490050","actor":{"login":"CaselIT","id":16175304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTc1MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16175304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT","html_url":"https://github.com/CaselIT","followers_url":"https://api.github